TRACK G CATALOGUE GRANTS, live project uccixoonmbhrnyczyigt, 2026-09-23.
Both blocks of scripts/probes/track_g_catalogue_grants.sql, run through
mcp__Supabase__apply_migration, each one transaction ended by a deliberate
raise exception so nothing was written.

--- BEFORE, run immediately prior to migration 20260923103430 -----------------

ERROR:  P0001: PROBE ALL PASS track-g-before, 8 assertions, 2 controls green.
THE PUBLIC CATALOGUE IS REFUSED 42501 TO anon AND TO authenticated over 64
published listings, because private.owns_listing lost EXECUTE on 22 September
while 17 RLS policies still call it. Separately anon holds no column privilege
on listings.listing_role, which both listing selects now name. And anon reads 0
rows of public.agents, so no lister name has a public door. Rolled back on
purpose.

The diagnostic run that found the cause, same tool, same day, before the probe
above was written:

ERROR:  P0001: DIAGNOSTIC: [id only: 42501 permission denied for function
owns_listing] [id+status: 42501 permission denied for function owns_listing]
[bare count(*): 42501 permission denied for function owns_listing] [policies:
listings_admin_all=*:(private.has_role((SELECT auth.uid() AS uid),
'admin'::app_role) OR private.has_role((SELECT auth.uid() AS uid),
'super_admin'::app_role)) | listings_owner_all=*:private.owns_listing(id) |
listings_select_published=r:(status = 'PUBLISHED'::listing_status)]

--- AFTER, run immediately following migration 20260923103430 ----------------

ERROR:  P0001: PROBE ALL PASS track-g-after, 10 assertions, 2 opposite-shape
controls green (anon still reads 0 agents rows and is still refused
listings.supply_verified_by). anon and a signed-in reader each read all 64
published listings including listing_role, every joined catalogue table reads,
a DRAFT row is filtered rather than fatal, and no table-wide or extra column
privilege appeared. Rolled back on purpose, the draft row is gone.

--- THE SURVEY THAT FOUND THE BLAST RADIUS ----------------------------------

Every function named in an RLS policy expression, joined to whether anon and
authenticated can execute it. Read from pg_proc and pg_policy, never from
information_schema. Four came back short on 2026-09-23:

  private.owns_listing(uuid)                     anon NO   authenticated NO
    17 policies: listing_videos_select, listing_videos_write,
    listing_access_select, listing_access_write_own, listing_access_update_own,
    listing_access_delete_own, listing_photos_select, listing_photos_write,
    listing_amenities_select, listing_amenities_write, availability_select,
    availability_write, reviews_select, inspection_requests_insert_requester,
    agent_documents_select_by_listing, listings_owner_all,
    listing_mandates_select_own, listing_mandates_insert_own

  private.attachment_path_access(text)           anon NO   authenticated yes
  private.can_see_listing_access(uuid)           anon NO   authenticated yes
  private.escrow_evidence_path_access(text,bool) anon NO   authenticated yes

Only the first was closed by 20260923103430, because only the first refuses a
read the product actually makes. The other three are latent hazards of the same
shape and are recorded in docs/BUILD_07_LEDGER.md rather than changed, because
widening a grant nobody has asked for is the mistake in the other direction.
